Title: Stephen Robinson left 'shocked' after St Mirren draw with Arbroath
Date: 2025-07-13
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Stephen Robinson', 'Text': '"I\'m in a little bit of shock," he told club media.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 43}}, {'Speaker': 'Stephen Robinson', 'Text': '"The performance of maybe 13 of them is something I\'ve not seen all pre-season. We\'ve had a fantastic pre-season.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 102}}, {'Speaker': 'Stephen Robinson', 'Text': '"I didn\'t recognise some of the decision-making, some of the passing, some of the simple things we\'ve continually done through the pre-season.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 125}}, {'Speaker': 'Stephen Robinson', 'Text': '"We decided as a collective not to do that and got exactly what we deserved.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 7, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 69}}, {'Speaker': 'Stephen Robinson', 'Text': '"We\'re not going to feel sorry for ourselves. It\'s disappointing for us, disappointing for the people that travelled a long way on a Saturday when they could have been sitting in the garden – I bet they wish they had done.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 8, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 184}}, {'Speaker': 'Stephen Robinson', 'Text': '"But it\'s a group of boys that have never let me down over a longer period of time. As I say, we have to be and will be better than that.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 9, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 119}}, {'Speaker': 'Stephen Robinson', 'Text': '"We have to react to it, we will be better. We have to do simple things which we didn\'t do."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 10, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 79}}], 'Description': [{'Description': '"Shocked" Stephen Robinson apologised to St Mirren fans who travelled to Arbroath for their Premier Sports Cup opener which ended in a goalless draw and a defeat on penalties.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 1, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 161}}, {'Description': 'St Mirren are back on the road on Tuesday, visiting League 2 Forfar Athletic and Robinson is demanding a response after he "didn\'t recognise" some of his side\'s play.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 143}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': "St Mirren Manager Stephen Robinson looks dejected following his side's defeat during a Premier Sports Cup group stage match between Arbroath and St Mirren at Gayfield Park"}]}
